# Packages installed into the Apus root filesystem (one per line).
base
archlinuxarm-keyring
linux-aarch64
mkinitcpio
dosfstools
less
nano

# A shell from the Mac, for debugging the machine while it runs. It lets
# nobody in by itself: root has no password, and a key only reaches the
# machine through the directory that the VM shares. See docs/building.md.
openssh

# Apus branding (packages/apus-release)
apus-release

# The Swift UI (packages/apus-ui, built from ui/)
apus-ui

# Vulkan, for a guest with a GPU. vulkan-virtio is Mesa's Venus driver: it
# turns Vulkan calls into a stream that the virtio-gpu device carries to the
# renderer on the Mac. vulkan-icd-loader is what an app links to.
# packages/vulkan-virtio builds this one, because Mesa's has to learn the
# step between blobs that a Mac needs. See docs/gpu.md.
vulkan-icd-loader
vulkan-virtio
# vulkaninfo, which tests/venus.exp reads to check that the guest found the
# GPU of the Mac.
vulkan-tools

# Zink (packages/apus-zink): OpenGL on Vulkan, so that the GLES of the
# compositor reaches the GPU of the Mac. The compositor asks for it by name.
apus-zink


# Sound. virtio-snd (packages/virtio-snd) is the driver of the sound card of
# the VM, which linux-aarch64 leaves out. PipeWire is the sound server, with
# WirePlumber to manage it, and pipewire-pulse and pipewire-alsa so that
# programs written for PulseAudio or for ALSA reach it too. alsa-utils has
# aplay and speaker-test, and the freedesktop sound theme gives the
# names of the system sounds and a set of them. See docs/audio.md.
virtio-snd
pipewire
wireplumber
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
alsa-utils
sound-theme-freedesktop
